# Compiles every CrossByte class that is available in a browser.
#
# There is no main and nothing is run: this asks the one question that rots
# fastest, which is whether the portable half of the framework still compiles
# without a filesystem, without threads and without a socket. A `Sys.` call
# added to a file nobody thought was platform-bound fails here and nowhere
# else, because every other target has a Sys.
#
# `include` pulls in the whole package tree, so a module excluded from the
# browser build is skipped rather than failing -- which is what makes the pass
# meaningful: everything not excluded has to compile.
-cp src
--macro include('crossbyte')
--js export/js/crossbyte.js
-D js-flatten
